      "mergeID": "64c9229d5bba83093a24ebd4",
      "mergedPostDetails": "1. Upload or find large avatar (200m is sufficient to see issue)\n\n2. Set up private instance with other player willing to test with\n\n3. Switch to large avatar\n\nExpected result: both players see avatar at same size\n\nActual result: player using avatar sees self at 200m, other player sees first player at 100m but floating 100m above ground.\n\nOnly tested on PC but likely happens on Quest as well.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Avatars larger than 100m do not show correctly to other players",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "64c4477f924afa290fa94709",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 4
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Tupper had said on twitter that \"You can still upload avatars of any size even we say we dont support this\".\n\nSo this likely is unintended behaviour on the remote users side. Really annoying that this is the case currently, i hope they fix it soon.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
